raph.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Request for Promotion to Senior Paralegal\n\nDear [Managing Partner's name],\n\nI am writing to ask you to consider me for promotion to senior paralegal in the litigation group. I have been a paralegal here for five years, and I believe my work, especially over the past year, shows I'm ready for the senior role.\n\n**Workload and results**\nLast year I supported four lawyers on 23 cases, two of which went to trial. I billed 1,640 hours, 90 more than the group's target of 1,550.\n\n**Training and team development**\nI trained all three paralegals the group has hired in the past two years. Since the senior role is mainly about supervising paralegals, this has given me direct experience getting new team members up to speed on our cases, procedures and systems.\n\n**Systems and risk management**\nIn 2023 I built the group's court-deadline tracking sheet. Two other groups at the firm have since adopted it.\n\nLast March, I entered a filing deadline incorrectly in that sheet. A colleague caught the error, and we filed two hours before the court's cutoff. I took that seriously. Afterward I added a second-person check to the sheet, so that a mistake like mine gets caught by the process and not by luck. I think the way I handled that mistake is part of my case for promotion. A senior paralegal should own errors and build safeguards that protect the whole team.\n\n**My request**\nI am asking to be promoted to senior paralegal, with the corresponding salary adjustment. I'm ready to take on formal supervision of the group's paralegals and to keep improving how we manage deadlines and workflow.\n\nI would welcome the chance to discuss this with you. Please let me know a time that works for you.\n\nThank you for your consideration.\n\nSincerely,\n[Your name]\n</final_document>\n\nThe letter is about 310 words. I mentioned the \"corresponding salary adjustment\" but left out the $9,000 figure. The partner already knows the pay difference, and putting the number in the opening request can make the letter sound like it's about money. You can easily add it if you want to be explicit.","ttft_ms":9474,"type":"result","duration_ms":16684,"uuid":"92edad5e-0297-47ff-b4c0-903ac3e65fea","ttft_stream_ms":947,"time_to_request_ms":188,"first_content_frame_ms":947,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":1584,"cacheReadInputTokens":3853,"cacheCreationInputTokens":5391,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0755866,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":820,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":5391,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-07T10:02:13.271Z"}
